# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Agent Operating Rules

This file is the law. The skills in `.claude/skills/` are the procedure that satisfies it. If a skill and this file ever conflict, this file wins.

Procedure lives in skills; this file only states what must hold and what enforces it. Anything here that grows into a paragraph of *how* belongs in a skill instead.

## Who reviews, and how

{{OWNER_NAME}} directs this project. Every checkpoint must produce something reviewable **without reading a diff**: a plain-English task-log entry, a UI walkthrough, an eval scorecard, an explicit chat confirmation. If a step can't be restated in those terms, redesign the step.

Does {{OWNER_NAME}} read code: {{OWNER_READS_CODE}}. The reviewable-artifact bar is the same either way; the answer only decides how much SQL and diff you show alongside it.

## Rules

Every rule names the trigger that runs it and the artifact that proves it ran. A rule missing any of the three columns is a defect that `scripts/check-rule-triggers.mjs` reports and CI blocks on.

