## Task tracking

**One file per task, in `tasks/`.** `TASKS.md` and `TASKS_ARCHIVE.md` are **generated indexes** — regenerate them, never edit them. Changing a task's state is editing one line of its own frontmatter; nothing moves between files.

A not-yet-started idea is a task file with `status: backlog`; `BACKLOG.md` is the generated index of the tasks in `backlog` and `todo`, and promoting one is changing that status. Anything carried between sessions that isn't a task yet goes in `PENDINGS.md`, with who can close it and how many sessions it has survived. Session logs live in `/logs/`; `STATUS.md` holds current state and references only the most recent one.


**Three places, three questions.** The task file says *where the work is going* — status, done-when, open blockers — and is corrected in place. A scope doc in `docs/` says *how it is built* — design, decisions, approved risks — and is corrected in place too, keeping dated decisions marked superseded rather than deleted. The task log, `logs/tasks/<id>.md`, says *what happened* — review rounds, findings, fixes, measurements, decisions, the approved adversarial cases — and only grows; the skills write it with `scripts/task-log-append.mjs`, and `logs/tasks/current/<id>.md` is its generated view. See `ae-kit-templates/task-log-ontology.md`.

This is {{OWNER_NAME}}'s primary review surface; keep it fast to scan.
